/*
    `where` is right-declarative: it introduces a local scope spanning the expression,
    the RIGHT operand declares into it, and the left operand refers to it.
    The value is the value of the left operand, on the condition that the right operand
    evaluates to true.
    This is how a name used on the left can be constrained after the fact.
*/

T * T ^^ T where T : (int | float)
